tellraw @s ["\n","\n"]

# Expirators
tellraw @s[scores={species=001}] [{"text":"+ Expirator +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=001}] ["\n","The Expirators, spiritual descendants of the infamous Enhanced, are augmented to be calm and cool-headed in all situations. As a result, when left alone, they prefer to lead very peaceful lives. However, their physical superiority leaves them ready to fight any challenge that might arise."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=001}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Evolution","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=001}] ["\n","When an Expirator reaches a certain XP threshold, they’re given an Expirator Shard, which can be consumed in order to Evolve. Evolution drains XP in order to increase base stats."]

# Forma
tellraw @s[scores={species=002}] [{"text":"+ Forma +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=002}] ["\n","The creative Forma have the unique ability to reshape and command earthen matter. This ability, thought to be descended from long-dead gods, has shaped Forma into a species of builders and architects. Having been around for a long, long time, Forma have grown quite attuned to the environment, and they learn much from birth through the knowledge passed down from their ancestors."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=002}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Creation","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=002}] ["\n","In any dimension, if a Forma holds some earthen blocks in their offhand, they can duplicate that block into their main hand by pressing the swap hands button (which is set to F by default). In the nether, they can perform this with netherrack as well, and in the end, they can do this with end stone."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=002}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Good Health","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=002}] ["\n","Forma will not lose hunger as long as they are at full health."]

# Paladins
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] [{"text":"+ Paladin +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","The Paladins, long-time defenders of peace and security, are an order of soldiers created by the divine Ascians. They’re innately talented in killing and harvesting monsters, and are also designed to be able to Link with golems, allowing both them and the golem to grow slightly in power. They can kill a golem to condense it into an egg, which can be cracked to birth another golem, stronger than the first."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Divine Looting","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","Paladins increase the drops of many monsters they kill."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","Paladins have positive effects from eating Rotten Flesh. Instead of gaining the hunger debuff, they become immune to hunger, poison, and slowness for the following minute. They also heal a tiny bit of health."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Ajnheil Link","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","Paladins can Link with Iron Golems within 20m of them. This will grant minor Resistance to both the Paladin and the Golem, and will ensure the Paladin’s food bar stays full. The Link will automatically deactivate if the distance between the Paladin and any Golem is more than 20m."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","If a Paladin kills an Iron Golem, they will be given a spawn egg that will spawn a new Iron Golem, called a Paladin Golem. Paladin Golems have 150% health and will not ever attack players, even if provoked. However, they also do not drop anything upon death, unless killed by a Paladin, in which case they’ll drop another Paladin Golem spawn egg."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=003}] ["\n","Paladins can pacify Golems, preventing them from ever attacking players (even if provoked), by holding a poppy and walking near the Golem."]

# Shadowbringers
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] [{"text":"+ Shadowbringer +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","Shadowbringers were originally designed for war, but after the completion of the war, they found themselves unsure where to go next. They retain the magics granted to them by their collective mother, but with no enemy to levy this magic against, what will they use it for?"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Shadow Step","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","While holding a Stone Sword, Shadowbringers can crouch to teleport a short distance forward."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Wither Touch","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","Shadowbringers are immune to Wither."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","They inflict Wither on all creatures they harm."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","Wither Roses heal them."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=004}] ["\n","Shadowbringers are friendly with Wither Skeletons."]

# Filoure
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] [{"text":"+ Filoure +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","Filouren, the proud, foxish Beastpeople of the northern lands, boast swiftness and agility in all areas, including combat. They’re impossibly hard to keep up with, let alone catch, and both their allies and enemies consider the signature Filouren swiftness their greatest strength."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Filouren Agility","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","Filouren are, by default, 30% faster than regular players."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","Filouren gain a brief burst of speed when dealing or taking damage. This effect will not trigger if the damage dealt or taken is nullified, whether by resistance, absorption, or something else. This will also not trigger if only a very small amount of damage is dealt/taken."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Grace","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","Filouren do not take fall damage from most falls. However, very long falls (~250+ blocks) will deal the normal amount of damage."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Chain Jumping","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","While sprinting, a Filoure’s jump height is tripled."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Carnivore","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=005}] ["\n","Filouren gain buffs from eating raw meat."]

# Feldspar
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] [{"text":"+ Feldspar +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","The Feldspari are a sturdy folk, and wear their near-immunity to death as a badge on their sleeve. They’re able to recover from wounds that would be fatal for anyone else, and they’re naturally hurt less, from all sources."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Sturdy Stagger","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"This ability is only active if Staggering is enabled.","italic":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","Feldspari can immediately recover from a Staggered state by healing back to full health. Feldspari can be Staggered infinitely per lifetime."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Alternative Ability: Sturdy Stagger II","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"This ability is active if Staggering is not enabled.","italic":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","Feldspari have an extra row of hearts, that do not naturally regenerate, but are fully refreshed when respawning or sleeping. These hearts wear off after one IRL hour, unless they’re refreshed."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Carnivore","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=006}] ["\n","Feldspari gain buffs from eating raw meat."]

# Homarach
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] [{"text":"+ Homarach +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","The Homarachi are a group of quadrupedal silkspinners, able to climb walls and ceilings as easily as you or I might stroll through a field. Traditionally, they’ve preferred reclusion, creating nest and dens full of sticky threads, that they can easily move through, but will heavily hinder any intruders. Many find them unnerving, although those who have interacted closely with Homarachi often speak highly of their wit and thoughtfulness. Of course, like any other species, it just depends on the individual."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Climber","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","Homarachi have the ability to scale any non-air block simply by standing next to it, looking at the surface they want to climb, and jumping. They can also crouch to descend instead of ascend. Homarachi can also climb across ceilings by staring straight up."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Trapper","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","Homarachi can move through spiderwebs extremely quickly, and their body becomes invisible inside a spider web. They also gain resistance."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Spider Friend","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=007}] ["\n","Homarachi are friendly to wild spiders, and are immune to poison."]

# Kamensh
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] [{"text":"+ Kamensh +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] ["\n","The Kamenshi have a long, rich history in Kingdom-occupied territories. Although their first experiences with the Kingdom resulted in their displacement, and the loss of their ancestral land, they have since moved on, with most Kamenshi moving to other continents and even other worlds. Despite their migration, Kamensh society still holds a widespread distaste for the Kingdom. Kamenshi are deeply attuned to the earth around them, and are able to navigate underground areas easily. They’re very wealthy, being able to squeeze every last granule of precious stone out of the earth they mine."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Ore Expert","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] ["\n","Kamenshi gain more resources when mining Deepslate ores. This can stack with Fortune."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] ["\n","Kamenshi gain experience from mining certain Deepslate-based blocks."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Denizen of the Depths","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=008}] ["\n","Kamenshi gain Haste, Speed, Night Vision, and Fire Resistance when below y = 0."]

# Myconid
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] [{"text":"+ Myconid +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","Myconids are extremely intelligent and deeply social creatures, able to settle down and create complex societies virtually anywhere. Being flora-based, they prefer natural foods, and feel most comfortable around their inanimate mushroom siblings. They’re able to release spores with many different effects, both helpful and harmful, depending on the situation."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Home Turf","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","Myconids gain saturation, resistance, haste, strength, and speed when on a natural mushroom island, or in specialized underground caves."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Fungal Flesh","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","Myconids are immune to hunger and poison."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","If two or more Myconids are within 30 blocks of each other, or if a Myconid is standing on Mycelium, they will regenerate a few hearts every five seconds."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","If Myconids have nothing in their main hand, and they’re standing on grass, podzol, or mycelium, they’ll grow a mushroom at their feet every couple seconds."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Shroom Spores","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","After taking damage, Myconids release a spore cloud that slows and weakens anyone who enters it. Myconids are immune to this cloud for a short while."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Decay Diet","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","Eating rotten flesh restores more hunger and some health."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=009}] ["\n","Eating mushroom stew restores some health, and grants brief resistance and haste."]

# Passidian
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] [{"text":"+ Passidian +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","The Passidian Empire is a strong submarine nation, governed by a council of representatives, with representatives representing each school of craft: architecture, construction, artistry, etc. Passidians are able to filter oxygen and nutrients from water, and as such, are able to breathe and thrive both underwater and on land, with an obvious preference for water. They also boast a membrane-like second skin, that’s able to regenerate using salt and minerals found in natural lakes and oceans. Ancient Passidians created the trident and pioneered trident combat, and current-day Passidians prefer to use tridents, both out of respect and honest preference."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Seaskin","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","Passidians can breathe and mine faster underwater. They also reduce 40% of all incoming damage while underwater."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","Every ten seconds spent underwater, Passidians regenerate a magical shell of armor, that protects from 2 hearts of damage before breaking."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Oceanic Blessing","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","Passidians deal 6 extra damage (subject to modifiers) per hit when using a Trident."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Piscivore","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=011}] ["\n","Passidians gain buffs from eating raw fish."]

# Noctian
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] [{"text":"+ Noctian +","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","The Noctian hails from a faraway land, and is plagued by the shadows of the past. Their body is reinforced with natural keratin, that lashes out in the heat of combat. Their origins have left them with unnatural abilities, allowing them to warp space and see beyond sight."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Sanguine Step","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","While holding any sword, the Noctian can crouch to teleport a short distance forward."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Strongarm","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","The Noctian has increased mining speed with any non-sword tools."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","The Noctian deals 1 extra damage per hit when using a sword."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Kertin","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","Upon dealing damage or blocking damage with a shield, the Noctian gains a brief period of increased damage."]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Night Sight","bold":true}]
tellraw @s[scores={species=019}] ["\n","The Noctian\\’s vision is vastly improved in the darkness."]

