# obsolete / unfinished
tellraw @s[scores={species=010}] [{"text":"+ Fawn +","bold":true},"\n","Fawns, the children of the forests, are typically quite shy, and use their natural camouflage to hide in treetops, tall grasses, bushes, and vegetations of all kind. Like their flora-based siblings, they prefer natural foods, such as fruits and berries. Fawns are able to borrow from the lifeforce of vegetation, and passively heal their body when nestled within the leaves of trees or bushes.","\n","\n",{"text":"Hold the species Stone, in your main hand, in one of your hotbar slots, and then crouch to view your species's skills.","italic":true,"color":"gray"},"\n"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=012}] [{"text":"+ Draconian +","bold":true},"\n","Draconians are all siblings, born from the Dracomother Hadeus. Their homeland is unknown, but they’re able to survive in space, so they often take to the skies and live on asteroids and moons. Although this seems impractical, Draconians have little to no need for real sustenance, as they survive often purely off of energy from their mother. When away from home, however, they must survive like normal creatures.","\n","\n",{"text":"Hold the species Stone, in your main hand, in one of your hotbar slots, and then crouch to view your species's skills.","italic":true,"color":"gray"},"\n"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=013}] [{"text":"+ Ghost +","bold":true},"\n","A Ghost is the spectral husk of what once was a living creature. Bodiless and weightless, Ghosts appear as a glowing silhouette of their living form. However, not everything about being a Ghost is bad. Despite their increased fragility, Ghosts are immune to all environmental dangers, and have the ability to become fully invisible, if they wish. If you want to find a Ghost, keep your eyes open for shadows, and keep your ears perked for whispers of a past life.","\n","\n",{"text":"Hold the species Stone, in your main hand, in one of your hotbar slots, and then crouch to view your species's skills.","italic":true,"color":"gray"},"\n"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=014}] [{"text":"+ Necrophant +","bold":true},"\n","A Necrophant is brought into being when an individual has killed so much that their body overflows with life and burns away, leaving them somewhere between life and death. Necrophants are able to steal lifeforce from those they kill, and use it to increase their own lifespan.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Ghost Skin","bold":true},"\n","- Necrophants gain 80% damage reduction as long as they’re not wearing ANY armor.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Flight","bold":true},"\n","- Necrophants can sprint in midair to begin gaining altitude, and can stop sprinting to slowly float downwards.","\n","- Crouch to stop floating, and drop at regular speed. This will deal fall damage.","\n","- Sprint off a ledge to maintain your altitude.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Wraith Rush","bold":true},"\n","- Necrophants have enhanced speed when NOT sprinting.","\n","- While sprinting, Necrophants gain increased attack damage and attack speed.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Phantom Hunger","bold":true},"\n","- Necrophants lose hunger at a vastly accelerated rate. When they drop to 0 hunger, they rapidly decay into nothing.","\n","- Necrophants cannot eat food, as it will cause them to decay. Instead, they must regain hunger by damaging other living creatures.","\n","\n"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=018}] [{"text":"+ Arcane Soldier +","bold":true},"\n","Arcanism is a long-lost practice of the enigmatic Ascians, and some believe its inception occurred even before the time of the Ascians. Arcane Soldiers, although rare, still seem to roam the worlds. They’re notorious for their incredible, some would even say mystical, skill with weaponry, and their volatility in combat. Remnants of an ancient order of defenders, they have raw combative skill woven into every particle of their being. Arcane Soldier are able to transform the experience they gain from their slain foes into arcane mana, and use it to empower themselves in combat. Boasting a wide array of skill with all weapons, Arcane Soldiers are the last people you want to find yourself in a fight with.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Arcane Knight","bold":true},"\n","- Arcane Soldiers have all abilities of Arcane Knights, other than “Sharpened Sword”.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Arcane Brigand","bold":true},"\n","- Arcane Soldiers have all abilities of Arcane Brigands, other than “Heavy Axe”.","\n","\n",{"text":"Ability: Arcane Archer","bold":true},"\n","- Arcane Soldiers have all abilities of Arcane Archers, other than “Turret Archer”.","\n","\n"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=022}] [{"text":"+ Incarnate +","bold":true},"\n","Incarnates are the fiery denizens of hell, the infernal defenders of their homeland. They wield and repel flame with unnatural ease, and are never strong than when they’re in their homeworld. Do not try to defeat an Incarnate when they’re on their home court. It will not go well.","\n","\n",{"text":"Hold the species Stone, in your main hand, in one of your hotbar slots, and then crouch to view your species's skills.","italic":true,"color":"gray"},"\n"]
tellraw @s[scores={species=023..}] ["\n","Species Stone Dialog is still being written for this species."]

